ms: walking from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", the first vertex on a cycle is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"root(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tailLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" steps away (Sage’s “preperiod”), on a cycle of "},{"code":"cycleLength(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices. For a permutation, "},{"code":"cycles","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is its cycle decomposition and every tail is zero."}]}}}